<iscomment>
    app_waitlist OVERRIDE of app_storefront_base product/components/addToCartProduct.

    A faithful copy of the base add-to-cart row, plus:
      - the app_waitlist client bundle registered once (assets.addJs),
      - the buy-box row tagged data-waitlist-atc and hidden server-side when the
        resolved variant is out of stock (so Notify Me takes its place), and
      - the Back-In-Stock "Notify Me" block appended after it.

    This is the SMALLEST base seam at the buy box that renders exactly once per
    PDP load: base client JS toggles the add-to-cart button's disabled state on
    variant change but does NOT re-fetch this partial, so the notify block is
    never duplicated. Overriding this component (rather than forking the whole
    productDetails.isml) keeps the SFRA-upgrade re-merge surface tiny.
</iscomment>
<isscript>
    var assets = require('*/cartridge/scripts/assets.js');
    assets.addJs('/js/waitlist.js');
</isscript>

<iscomment>
    Show Notify Me for an out-of-stock unit that is either (a) a fully resolved
    variant, or (b) a variation MASTER with no orderable variants at all. Case
    (b) matters because base SFRA greys out every OOS variation value, so a
    wholly sold-out master can never resolve a variant from the dropdown -- a
    dead end without this fallback. A master's `available` is the AGGREGATE
    orderability, so `productType==='master' && !available` means precisely
    "zero orderable variants". The subscription is keyed to the master id; the
    notify job's aggregate isInStock() fires when ANY variant is replenished.
</iscomment>
<isset name="wlNotify" value="${!product.available && product.productType !== 'set' && product.productType !== 'bundle' && (product.readyToOrder || product.productType === 'master')}" scope="page" />

<div class="row cart-and-ipay${wlNotify ? ' d-none' : ''}" data-waitlist-atc>
    <div class="col-sm-12">
        <input type="hidden" class="add-to-cart-url" value="${pdict.addToCartUrl}">
        <button class="add-to-cart btn btn-primary"
                data-pid="${product.id}"
                ${!product.readyToOrder || !product.available ? "disabled" : ""}>
            <i class="fa fa-shopping-bag"></i>
            ${Resource.msg('button.addtocart', 'common', null)}
        </button>

        <isinclude template="product/components/addToCartButtonExtension"/>
    </div>
</div>

<isinclude template="product/waitlistNotify" />
